# UI conventions

Details: `docs/design/` (read the topic file you are changing).

## Tokens
- Color by role: `bg-surface`, `bg-surface-muted`, `text-ink`, `text-ink-muted`, `border-border`, `bg-primary-700`, `text-primary-700`, `hover:text-accent`, `hover:bg-accent`.
- Accent (crimson) only for hover, focus, and current state. Secondary gold (`bg-secondary-50/100`, `border-secondary`) only as a background behind dark text or a decorative bar; never text, outlines, or buttons.
- Radius `rounded-control` (controls) and `rounded-card` (cards). Shadow `shadow-card` only on cards.
- No hex, `rgb()`, arbitrary values (`bg-[#...]`, `text-[17px]`), or raw palette colors (`bg-blue-600`, `text-gray-500`).

## Typography
- Use `h1`-`h3` elements and their base styles; do not restyle per page. One `h1` per page, no skipped levels.
- Body text at least `text-base`; `text-sm` only for metadata.
- Long text in `<Container width="reading">`; article bodies in `.prose-content`.

## Layout
- Use `Container` for width and padding, never hand-written `mx-auto max-w-* px-*`.
- Mobile first; Tailwind default breakpoints only. Sections `py-16`, grids `gap-6`.
- Prefer logical utilities: `ms-`/`me-`, `ps-`/`pe-`, `start-`/`end-`, `text-start`, `border-s`.
- No fixed heights on text; no horizontal scroll at 320px.

## Buttons and links
```astro
<!-- Good: action -->
<Button type="submit">Send inquiry</Button>
<!-- Good: moving between content pages -->
<a href="/articles/" class="text-primary-700 hover:text-accent font-medium">Read articles</a>
<!-- Bad: button styling for ordinary content navigation -->
<Button href="/articles/" variant="secondary">View all</Button>
```
- At most one `variant="primary"` per view. Labels start with a verb.
- `Button href` only when a link is the view's single main action. The home welcome banner's "Read articles" is the current case; see `docs/design/buttons.md`.
- Only `primary` and `secondary` variants exist; do not add one-off button styles.

## Cards
- Cards only on listing and hub pages, inside `<ul class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">`.
- The heading link is the only control. No wrapping `<a>` around the card, no `after:absolute after:inset-0` overlay.
- Pass the correct `headingLevel` for the page outline.

## Logo
- Only in the header (and the favicon/share image via `Seo`), not the footer, from `assets/logo/logo.jpg` with `<Image>`; alt is `site.name`. Details: `docs/design/navigation.md#logo`.
- No text wordmark, tagline, rating, or trust badge beside it. Do not crop, recolor, or stretch it, or use it as a hero.

## Footer
- One slim `bg-primary-700` bar: copyright at the start, then Line, Viber, Messenger, Facebook icon links from `socialLinks` in `src/lib/site.ts`. No logo, no repeated navigation, no other networks.
- Icon links are `size-11` with `sr-only` names; white, `hover:text-secondary`, `focus-visible:outline-white`. Viber's icon opens a `<details>` list of numbers (`ViberNumbers`) above it. Details: `docs/design/navigation.md#footer`.

## Accessibility
- WCAG 2.2 AA contrast; never remove the global `:focus-visible` outline.
- Touch targets at least 44px (`size-11` for icon buttons); icon-only controls need `sr-only` text.
- Do not convey meaning by color alone. Sections with headings use `aria-labelledby`.

## Home banner illustration
- `Skyline` (`src/components/home/Skyline.astro`) is home-only: the decorative `<Picture>` (`alt=""`, `priority`). Below `lg` the banner fills the first screen (`min-h-first-screen`); from `lg` its height follows the picture's 16:10 shape, never the screen height, so the image is not enlarged. Keep `sizes` equal to the drawn width. Text sits on the gold panel beside it (from `lg`) or below it, never on the picture. The panel opens with `site.slogan` (Burmese on both locales, `lang="my"`); show the slogan nowhere else. Details: `docs/design/layout.md#home-welcome-banner`.

## Home how-it-works
- `HowItWorks` (`src/components/home/HowItWorks.astro`) is home-only: an `<ol>` of six steps, not cards or links. One column with a dashed rail below `lg`, two rows of three from `lg`; never six in one row. Copy lives under `home.steps.*`. Details: `docs/design/layout.md#home-how-it-works-section`.

## Home hospital strip
- `HospitalStrip` (`src/components/home/HospitalStrip.astro`) is home-only, between the banner and `HowItWorks`: the same header as `HowItWorks` (centered `h2` `home.hospitals.title`, `bg-primary-700` bar, `text-lg` lead `home.hospitals.lead`) and one full-width row of logos drifting slowly (48s loop, CSS only, list rendered twice with the copy `aria-hidden`). It is the site's only moving element; do not copy it to other pages or add arrows, dots, or slides.
- It pauses on hover and keyboard focus; there is no pause button, by the site owner's choice. Under reduced motion it is a still, wrapping row. Logos load `eager` with `fetchpriority="low"` so they are ready before they slide in.
- Hospitals live in `src/lib/hospitals.ts` (name, trimmed logo from `assets/hospitals/`, optional `href`). No `href` means an unlinked image, never `href="#"`; with one, the logo links to the official site in a new tab, followed by an `sr-only` `common.opensInNewTab` label. Alt is the English hospital name. Accreditation claims in the lead still need a named body and a verification link once hospital pages exist. Details: `docs/design/layout.md#home-hospital-strip`.

## Avoid
Hero search boxes, carousels (the home hospital strip is the one exception), sticky inquiry bars, pop-ups, decorative animation, photos behind hero text, stock photos as real people or facilities, ads beside clinical content.
